Article 9 An advertisement shall not contain any of the following circumstances:
(1) Using or indirectly using the national flag, national anthem, or national emblem of the People's Republic of China, or the military flag, military anthem, or military emblem;
(2) Using or indirectly using the name or image of state organs or functionaries of state organs;
(3) Using such wording as "national-level", "highest-level", or "best";
(4) Damaging the dignity or interests of the state, or disclosing state secrets;
(5) Impairing social stability, or harming the public interest;
(6) Endangering personal or property safety, or disclosing personal privacy;
(7) Impairing public order or violating good social customs;
(8) Containing obscene, pornographic, gambling, superstitious, terror, or violent content;
(9) Containing content discriminating against ethnic groups, races, religions, or genders;
(10) Impairing the protection of the environment, natural resources, or cultural heritage;
(11) Other circumstances prohibited by laws or administrative regulations.

Article 16 Advertisements for medical treatment, drugs, and medical devices shall not contain the following content:
(1) Assertions or guarantees of efficacy or safety;
(2) Statements of cure rates or effectiveness rates;
(3) Comparisons with the efficacy and safety of other drugs or medical devices, or with other medical institutions;
(4) Using advertising endorsers for recommendations or certifications;
(5) Other content prohibited by laws or administrative regulations.
The content of drug advertisements shall be consistent with the instructions approved by the drug regulatory department of the State Council, and shall prominently indicate contraindications and adverse reactions. Prescription drug advertisements shall prominently indicate "This advertisement is for reading by medical and pharmaceutical professionals only", and non-prescription drug advertisements shall prominently indicate "Please purchase and use in accordance with the drug instructions or under the guidance of a pharmacist".
Advertisements for medical devices recommended for personal use shall prominently indicate "Please read the product instructions carefully or purchase and use under the guidance of medical personnel". Where the medical device product registration certification documents contain contraindicated content or precautions, the advertisement shall prominently indicate "See the instructions for details on contraindicated content or precautions".

Article 18 Advertisements for health foods shall not contain the following content:
(1) Assertions or guarantees of efficacy or safety;
(2) Involving disease prevention or treatment functions;
(3) Claiming or implying that the advertised commodity is essential for ensuring health;
(4) Comparing with drugs or other health foods;
(5) Using advertising endorsers for recommendations or certifications;
(6) Other content prohibited by laws or administrative regulations.
Health food advertisements shall prominently indicate "This product cannot replace drugs".

Article 21: Advertisements for pesticides, veterinary drugs, feed and feed additives shall not contain the following:
(1) Assertions or guarantees regarding efficacy or safety;
(2) Use of the name or image of a scientific research institution, academic institution, technology extension institution, trade association, or professionals or users for recommendations or endorsements;
(3) Statements of effectiveness rates;
(4) Text, language or images that violate safety use regulations;
(5) Other content prohibited by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 23: Alcoholic beverage advertisements shall not contain the following:
(1) Inducing or encouraging drinking, or promoting excessive drinking;
(2) Depicting the act of drinking;
(3) Showing activities such as driving vehicles, boats, or aircraft;
(4) Expressly or impliedly stating that drinking has effects such as relieving tension and anxiety, or increasing physical strength.

Article 24: Education and training advertisements shall not contain the following:
(1) Express or implied guaranteed commitments regarding progression to higher education, passing examinations, obtaining academic degrees or diplomas, or qualification certificates, or regarding the effects of education or training;
(2) Express or implied statements that relevant examination institutions, their staff, or examination question setters are involved in the education or training;
(3) Use of the name or image of a scientific research institution, academic institution, education institution, trade association, professionals, or beneficiaries for recommendations or endorsements.

Article 25: Advertisements for goods or services such as investment promotion that carry expectations of investment returns shall provide reasonable reminders or warnings regarding possible risks and the bearing of risk liability, and shall not contain the following:
(1) Guaranteed commitments regarding future results, returns or related circumstances, expressly or impliedly indicating guaranteed principal, no risk, or guaranteed returns, except where otherwise provided by the State;
(2) Use of the name or image of an academic institution, trade association, professionals, or beneficiaries for recommendations or endorsements.

Article 26: For real estate advertisements, the housing information shall be truthful, the area shall be stated as the gross floor area or the floor area within the unit, and it shall not contain the following:
(1) Commitments regarding appreciation or investment returns;
(2) Representation of the project's location by the time required to reach a specific reference point;
(3) Violation of the State regulations on price management;
(4) Misleading publicity regarding planned or under-construction transportation, commercial, cultural and educational facilities, and other municipal conditions.

Article 27: Advertisements for crop seeds, forest tree seeds, grass seeds, breeding livestock and poultry, aquatic fry and fingerlings, and planting and breeding shall present statements regarding variety names, production performance, growth volume or yield, quality, resistance, special use value, economic value, and suitable planting or breeding scope and conditions in a truthful, clear and explicit manner, and shall not contain the following:
(1) Assertions that cannot be scientifically verified;
(2) Assertions or guarantees regarding efficacy;
(3) Analysis, predictions, or guaranteed commitments regarding economic benefits;
(4) Use of the name or image of a scientific research institution, academic institution, technology extension institution, trade association, or professionals or users for recommendations or endorsements.

Article 28: An advertisement that uses false or misleading content to deceive or mislead consumers constitutes a false advertisement.
An advertisement shall be considered false under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The goods or services do not exist;
(2) Information such as the performance, function, origin, use, quality, specifications, ingredients, price, producer, expiry date, sales status, or awards received of the goods, or the content, provider, form, quality, price, sales status, or awards received of the services, or promises related to the goods or services, is inconsistent with the actual situation and has a material impact on purchasing decisions;
(3) Using fabricated, forged, or unverifiable scientific research results, statistical data, survey results, abstracts, quotations, or other information as evidentiary materials;
(4) Fabricating the effects of using goods or receiving services;
(5) Other circumstances where false or misleading content is used to deceive or mislead consumers.

Article 42 Under any of the following circumstances, no outdoor advertisement shall be set up:
(1) Utilizing traffic safety facilities or traffic signs;
(2) Affecting the use of municipal public facilities, traffic safety facilities, traffic signs, fire-fighting facilities, or fire safety signs;
(3) Obstructing production or people's daily life, or damaging the appearance of a city or town;
(4) Setting up within the building control areas of state organs, protected cultural relics sites, scenic spots, etc., or within areas where the local people's government at or above the county level prohibits the setting up of outdoor advertisements.

Article 49 The market supervision and administration department, in performing its duties of advertising supervision and administration, may exercise the following powers:
(1) Conducting on-site inspection of places suspected of engaging in illegal advertising activities;
(2) Interrogating the party suspected of illegal activities or its legal representative, principal responsible person, and other relevant persons, and investigating the relevant units or individuals;
(3) Requiring the party suspected of illegal activities to provide relevant supporting documents within a specified time limit;
(4) Consulting and copying contracts, bills, account books, advertising works, and other relevant materials related to the suspected illegal advertisements;
(5) Sealing up or seizing property such as advertising articles, business tools, and equipment directly related to the suspected illegal advertisements;
(6) Ordering the suspension of publication of suspected illegal advertisements that may cause serious consequences;
(7) Other powers provided by laws and administrative regulations.
The market supervision and administration department shall establish and improve an advertising monitoring system, improve monitoring measures, and promptly discover and investigate and deal with illegal advertising acts according to law.

Article 57 Where any of the following acts is committed, the market supervision and administration department shall order the cessation of publication of the advertisement, impose a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan on the advertiser; if the circumstances are serious, the business license may be revoked, and the advertisement examination authority shall revoke the advertisement examination approval document and shall not accept its application for advertisement examination within one year; for the advertisement operator or advertisement publisher, the market supervision and administration department shall confiscate the advertising expenses, impose a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, the business license may also be revoked:
(1) Publishing an advertisement that contains the prohibited circumstances provided in Articles 9 and 10 of this Law;
(2) Publishing an advertisement for prescription drugs, pharmaceutical precursor chemicals, medical devices and treatment methods for drug addiction treatment in violation of Article 15 of this Law;
(3) Publishing an advertisement claiming that infant dairy products, beverages, and other foods can completely or partially replace breast milk in violation of Article 20 of this Law;
(4) Publishing a tobacco advertisement in violation of Article 22 of this Law;
(5) Using advertisements to promote products prohibited from production or sale or services prohibited from provision, or goods or services prohibited from being advertised, in violation of Article 37 of this Law;
(6) In violation of Paragraph 1 of Article 40 of this Law, publishing advertisements for medical treatments, pharmaceuticals, health foods, medical devices, cosmetics, alcoholic beverages, or beauty treatments, as well as online game advertisements detrimental to the physical and mental health of minors, on mass media targeting minors.

Article 58 Where any of the following acts is committed, the market supervision and administration department shall order the cessation of publication of the advertisement, order the advertiser to eliminate the effects within the corresponding scope, and impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than three times the advertising expenses; if the advertising expenses cannot be calculated or are obviously low, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than three times but not more than five times the advertising expenses shall be imposed; if the advertising expenses cannot be calculated or are obviously low, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed, and the business license may be revoked, and the advertisement examination authority shall revoke the advertisement examination approval document and shall not accept its application for advertisement examination within one year:
(1) Publishing an advertisement for medical treatments, pharmaceuticals, or medical devices in violation of Article 16 of this Law;
(2) Involving the therapeutic function of diseases in an advertisement, or using medical terms or terms that may confuse the promoted goods with pharmaceuticals or medical devices, in violation of Article 17 of this Law;
(3) Publishing an advertisement for health foods in violation of Article 18 of this Law;
(4) Publishing an advertisement for pesticides, veterinary drugs, feed, or feed additives in violation of Article 21 of this Law;
(5) Publishing an advertisement for alcoholic beverages in violation of Article 23 of this Law;
(6) Publishing an advertisement for education or training in violation of Article 24 of this Law;
(7) Publishing an advertisement for goods or services such as investment promotion that imply investment return expectations in violation of Article 25 of this Law;
(8) Publishing an advertisement for real estate in violation of Article 26 of this Law;
(9) Publishing an advertisement for crop seeds, forest tree seeds, grass seeds, breeding livestock and poultry, aquatic seedlings, and breeding and cultivation in violation of Article 27 of this Law;
(10) Using a minor under the age of 10 as an advertising spokesperson in violation of Paragraph 2 of Article 38 of this Law;
(11) Using a natural person, legal person, or other organization as an advertising spokesperson in violation of Paragraph 3 of Article 38 of this Law;
(12) Publishing advertisements in primary and secondary schools or kindergartens, or using items related to primary and secondary school students or young children, in violation of Article 39 of this Law;
(13) Publishing advertisements for goods or services targeting minors under the age of 14 in violation of Paragraph 2 of Article 40 of this Law;
(14) Publishing an advertisement without examination in violation of Article 46 of this Law.
Where a medical institution commits the illegal act as provided in the preceding paragraph and the circumstances are serious, in addition to the punishment imposed by the market supervision and administration department in accordance with this Law, the health administrative department may revoke the diagnosis and treatment subjects or the practice license of the medical institution.
Where an advertisement operator or advertisement publisher, knowing or should know of the illegal act provided in the first paragraph of this Article, still designs, produces, acts as an agent, or publishes it, the market supervision and administration department shall confiscate the advertising expenses and impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than three times the advertising expenses; if the advertising expenses cannot be calculated or are obviously low, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than three times but not more than five times the advertising expenses shall be imposed; if the advertising expenses cannot be calculated or are obviously low, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed, and the relevant department may suspend the advertisement publication business or revoke the business license.

Article 59 Where any of the following acts is committed, the market supervision and administration department shall order the cessation of publication of the advertisement and impose a fine of not more than 100,000 yuan on the advertiser:
(1) The content of the advertisement violates Article 8 of this Law;
(2) The cited content in the advertisement violates Article 11 of this Law;
(3) An advertisement involving patents violates Article 12 of this Law;
(4) The advertisement disparages the goods or services of other producers or business operators in violation of Article 13 of this Law.
Where an advertisement operator or advertisement publisher, knowing or should know of the illegal act provided in the preceding paragraph, still designs, produces, acts as an agent, or publishes it, the market supervision and administration department shall impose a fine of not more than 100,000 yuan.
Where an advertisement violates Article 14 of this Law by lacking identifiability, or violates Article 19 of this Law by publishing advertisements for medical treatments, pharmaceuticals, medical devices, or health foods in disguised form, the market supervision and administration department shall order rectification and impose a fine of not more than 100,000 yuan on the advertisement publisher.

Article 61 Where an advertising endorser falls under any of the following circumstances, the market supervision and administration department shall confiscate the illegal gains and impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than two times the illegal gains:
(1) violating the provisions of Article 16, paragraph 1, item (4) of this Law by making recommendations or certifications in advertisements for medical treatments, pharmaceuticals, or medical devices;
(2) violating the provisions of Article 18, paragraph 1, item (5) of this Law by making recommendations or certifications in advertisements for health foods;
(3) violating the provisions of Article 38, paragraph 1 of this Law by making recommendations or certifications for goods that the endorser has not used or services that the endorser has not received;
(4) knowing or should have known that the advertisement is false, still making recommendations or certifications for goods or services in the advertisement.

Article 68 Advertisers, advertising operators, and advertising publishers who, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commit any of the following torts shall bear civil liability according to law:
(1) harming the physical or mental health of minors or disabled persons in advertisements;
(2) counterfeiting the patents of others;
(3) disparaging the goods or services of other producers or business operators;
(4) using the name or image of another person without consent in advertisements;
(5) other infringements upon the lawful civil rights and interests of others.
